"default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279098219,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-03-14T03:57:56Z","updated_at":"2025-03-17T14:04:46Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nOnly tested in 4.4\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.4.stable - Debian GNU/Linux 12 (bookworm) 12 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated AMD Radeon Graphics (RADV GFX1103_R1) - AMD Ryzen 7 PRO 7840U w/ Radeon 780M Graphics (16 threads)\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen a signal is linked to a function, godot typically keeps track of this connection and makes it easy to navigate, using interactive indicators. If that function is inside of an inherited class, godot seems to get confused, even though the application continues to build and run without any problem.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Created a scene with signals pointing to local function\n2. Moved function into a separate class file\n3. The application can still be built, but godot cannot find the connected function.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[issue_demo.tar.gz](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/19240928/issue_demo.tar.gz)\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/47c4376f-95c3-48ad-b2ee-17d68ff08cda)","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104101/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hoo